IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-definitions`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation in force 6 May to 20 October 2026
-- (a rendering, not the official text). Part 5 Division 2: s 149B (appointment by ordinary resolution), s 150 (appointments voted on individually),
-- s 151 (validity of acts), s 152 (removal of directors). s 153 is shown repealed (a coverage row only).
-- Whether the company is private is the seat input `the company is a private company`; the keel's s 4(1) "public company" turns it into
-- the test these sections use. JUST TRUE yes; JUST FALSE the text says no in its own words; NOTHING the text does not say.

§ `Section 149B: appointment of directors by ordinary resolution`

-- Unless the constitution otherwise provides, a company may appoint a director by ordinary resolution passed at a general meeting.
-- src:12238 | 149B. Unless the constitution otherwise provides, a company may
-- src:12239 | appoint a director by ordinary resolution passed at a general meeting.
@ref s 149B (src:12238-12239)
GIVEN `the constitution otherwise provides` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the kind of resolution passed` IS A `Kind of resolution`
      `the resolution was passed at a general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 149B the company may appoint a director by ordinary resolution passed at a general meeting` MEANS
    IF `the constitution otherwise provides`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Unless the constitution otherwise provides" hands the question to the constitution, which is not among the sources; a grant ("may") whose "unless" gate is met by the constitution (grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork line in NOTES.md)
    ELSE (IF `the kind of resolution passed` EQUALS `an ordinary resolution` AND `the resolution was passed at a general meeting`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may appoint a director by ordinary resolution passed at a general meeting" names one way and does not say no to another

§ `Section 150: appointment of directors to be voted on individually`

-- (1), with (4) and (5): at a general meeting of a public company, a motion for the appointment of 2 or more persons as directors by a single
-- resolution must not be made unless a resolution that it may be so made has first been agreed to without any vote against.
-- (5): nothing in the section applies to a resolution altering the constitution or prevents the election of 2 or more directors by ballot or poll; subsection (1) takes this as its exception.
-- src:12267 | (5) Nothing in this section —
-- src:12269 | (a) applies to a resolution altering the company’s constitution;
-- src:12271 | (b) prevents the election of 2 or more directors by ballot or
-- src:12272 | poll.
@ref s 150(5) (src:12267-12272)
GIVEN `the resolution alters the company's constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors are elected by ballot or poll` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 150(5) nothing in section 150 applies to the resolution or prevents the election` MEANS
    IF `the resolution alters the company's constitution` OR `the directors are elected by ballot or poll`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Nothing in this section -- (a) applies to a resolution altering the company's constitution; (b) prevents the election of 2 or more directors by ballot or poll" names two cases and says nothing of the rest

-- src:12245 | 150.—(1) At a general meeting of a public company, a motion for
-- src:12246 | the appointment of 2 or more persons as directors by a single
-- src:12247 | resolution must not be made unless a resolution that it may be so
-- src:12248 | made has first been agreed to by the meeting without any vote being
-- src:12249 | given against it.
@ref s 150(1) (src:12245-12249)
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of persons whose appointment as directors the motion proposes` IS A NUMBER
      `the motion proposes their appointment by a single resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the motion is for the appointment of the persons, or for approving or nominating them for appointment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a resolution that the motion may be so made has first been agreed to by the meeting without any vote being given against it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution alters the company's constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors are elected by ballot or poll` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 150(1) the section bars the motion for the appointment of 2 or more persons as directors by a single resolution` MEANS
    IF NOT (`s 4(1) "public company" the company is a public company` TRUE `the company is a private company` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "At a general meeting of a public company" -- a scope limit with no "only"
    ELSE (IF NOT (`the number of persons whose appointment as directors the motion proposes` AT LEAST 2 AND `the motion proposes their appointment by a single resolution` AND `the motion is for the appointment of the persons, or for approving or nominating them for appointment`)
          THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a motion for the appointment of 2 or more persons as directors by a single resolution" (with subsection (4): a motion for approving or nominating counts) -- a scope limit with no "only"
          ELSE (IF `s 150(5) nothing in section 150 applies to the resolution or prevents the election` `the resolution alters the company's constitution` `the directors are elected by ballot or poll` EQUALS JUST TRUE
                THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section -- (a) applies to a resolution altering the company's constitution; (b) prevents the election of 2 or more directors by ballot or poll" (subsection (5))
                ELSE (IF `a resolution that the motion may be so made has first been agreed to by the meeting without any vote being given against it`
                      THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not be made unless a resolution that it may be so made has first been agreed to by the meeting without any vote being given against it" -- the "unless" is met
                      ELSE JUST TRUE)))

-- src:12254 | (2) A resolution passed pursuant to a motion made in contravention
-- src:12255 | of this section is void, whether or not its being so moved was objected
-- src:12256 | to at the time.
@ref s 150(2) (src:12254-12256)
GIVEN `the motion was made in contravention of section 150(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 150(2) the resolution passed pursuant to the motion is void` MEANS
    IF `the motion was made in contravention of section 150(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- whether or not its being so moved was objected to at the time
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A resolution passed pursuant to a motion made in contravention of this section is void" says nothing of a resolution passed on a motion made in compliance

-- src:12258 | (3) Where a resolution pursuant to a motion made in contravention
-- src:12259 | of this section is passed, no provision for the automatic
-- src:12260 | re‑appointment of retiring directors in default of another
-- src:12261 | appointment is to apply.
@ref s 150(3) (src:12258-12261)
GIVEN `a resolution pursuant to a motion made in contravention of section 150 is passed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 150(3) a provision for the automatic re-appointment of retiring directors in default of another appointment applies` MEANS
    IF `a resolution pursuant to a motion made in contravention of section 150 is passed`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no provision for the automatic re-appointment of retiring directors in default of another appointment is to apply"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a resolution pursuant to a motion made in contravention of this section is passed" -- a scope limit

-- src:12263 | (4) For the purposes of this section, a motion for approving a
-- src:12264 | person’s appointment or for nominating a person for appointment is
-- src:12265 | to be treated as a motion for the person’s appointment.
@ref s 150(4) (src:12263-12265)
GIVEN `the motion is for approving a person's appointment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the motion is for nominating a person for appointment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 150(4) the motion is treated as a motion for the person's appointment` MEANS
    IF `the motion is for approving a person's appointment` OR `the motion is for nominating a person for appointment`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a motion for approving a person's appointment or for nominating a person for appointment is to be treated as a motion for the person's appointment" names two kinds of motion

§ `Section 151: validity of acts of directors and officers`

DECLARE `s 151 who acted` IS ONE OF
    `s 151 a director`
    `s 151 a chief executive officer`
    `s 151 a secretary`
    `s 151 someone else`

-- src:12278 | 151. The acts of a director or chief executive officer or secretary are
-- src:12279 | valid despite any defect that may afterwards be discovered in his or
-- src:12280 | her appointment or qualification.
@ref s 151 (src:12278-12280)
GIVEN `who acted` IS A `s 151 who acted`
      `a defect is afterwards discovered in the person's appointment or qualification` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 151 the act is valid despite a defect in the appointment or qualification of the person who did it` MEANS
    IF `who acted` EQUALS `s 151 someone else`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The acts of a director or chief executive officer or secretary" names three offices
    ELSE (IF `a defect is afterwards discovered in the person's appointment or qualification`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "despite any defect that may afterwards be discovered in his or her appointment or qualification" speaks only of such a defect

§ `Section 152: removal of directors`

-- (1) a public company may by ordinary resolution remove a director before the expiration of his or her period of office, despite anything in its constitution or in any agreement.
-- src:12286 | 152.—(1) A public company may by ordinary resolution remove a
-- src:12287 | director before the expiration of his or her period of office, despite
-- src:12288 | anything in its constitution or in any agreement between it and the
-- src:12289 | director but where any director so removed was appointed to
-- src:12290 | represent the interests of any particular class of shareholders or
-- src:12291 | debenture holders the resolution to remove the director does not take
-- src:12292 | effect until the director’s successor has been appointed.
@ref s 152(1) (src:12286-12292)
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the kind of resolution passed` IS A `Kind of resolution`
      `the director is removed before the expiration of his or her period of office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 152(1) the public company may remove the director by ordinary resolution` MEANS
    IF `s 4(1) "public company" the company is a public company` TRUE `the company is a private company` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the kind of resolution passed` EQUALS `an ordinary resolution` AND `the director is removed before the expiration of his or her period of office`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- despite anything in the constitution or in any agreement between the company and the director
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A public company may by ordinary resolution remove a director before the expiration of his or her period of office" -- a grant ("may") limited to a public company, an ordinary resolution and removal before expiry (grant ruling of 2026-11-12; fork line in NOTES.md)

-- (1) where the director removed was appointed to represent the interests of a class of shareholders or debenture holders, the resolution does not take effect until the successor is appointed
-- ("until" bar, ruling (d) of 2026-11-05: JUST TRUE before the successor is appointed, JUST FALSE after).
@ref s 152(1) (src:12290-12292)
GIVEN `the director removed was appointed to represent the interests of a particular class of shareholders or debenture holders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director's successor has been appointed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 152(1) the resolution to remove the director cannot yet take effect` MEANS
    IF `the director removed was appointed to represent the interests of a particular class of shareholders or debenture holders`
    THEN (IF `the director's successor has been appointed`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the resolution to remove the director does not take effect until the director's successor has been appointed" -- the "until" is met
          ELSE JUST TRUE)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where any director so removed was appointed to represent the interests of any particular class" -- a scope limit with no "only"

-- (2) special notice is required of a resolution to remove a director of a public company, or to appoint someone in the director's place at the same meeting.
-- src:12296 | (2) Special notice is required of any resolution to remove a director
-- src:12297 | of a public company under subsection (1) or to appoint some person
-- src:12298 | in place of a director so removed at the meeting at which the director
-- src:12299 | is removed, and on receipt of notice of an intended resolution to
-- src:12300 | remove a director under subsection (1) the company must
-- src:12305 | immediately send a copy thereof to the director concerned, and the
-- src:12306 | director, whether or not he or she is a member of the company, is
-- src:12307 | entitled to be heard on the resolution at the meeting.
@ref s 152(2) (src:12296-12307)
GIVEN `the resolution is to remove a director of a public company under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution is to appoint some person in place of a director so removed at the meeting at which the director is removed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 152(2) special notice is required of the resolution` MEANS
    IF `the resolution is to remove a director of a public company under subsection (1)` OR `the resolution is to appoint some person in place of a director so removed at the meeting at which the director is removed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Special notice is required of any resolution to remove a director of a public company under subsection (1) or to appoint some person in place of a director so removed" names two resolutions

@ref s 152(2) (src:12299-12307)
GIVEN `the company has received notice of an intended resolution to remove a director under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 152(2) the company must immediately send a copy of the notice to the director concerned` MEANS
    IF `the company has received notice of an intended resolution to remove a director under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on receipt of notice of an intended resolution to remove a director under subsection (1) the company must immediately send a copy thereof to the director concerned" -- an "on receipt" gate (ruling (c) of 2026-11-05 counts "upon" as "where") that fails

@ref s 152(2) (src:12305-12307)
GIVEN `the company has received notice of an intended resolution to remove a director under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 152(2) the director is entitled to be heard on the resolution at the meeting` MEANS
    IF `the company has received notice of an intended resolution to remove a director under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- whether or not the director is a member of the company
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on receipt of notice of an intended resolution to remove a director under subsection (1) ... the director, whether or not he or she is a member of the company, is entitled to be heard" -- an "on receipt" gate that fails; an "entitled" function: group (iii) of the grant ruling, fork line in NOTES.md

-- (3) where the director makes written representations (not exceeding a reasonable length) and asks for them to be notified to members, the company must, unless received too late,
-- state the fact in the notice and send a copy to every member to whom notice of the meeting is sent.
-- src:12311 | (3) Where notice is given pursuant to subsection (2) and the director
-- src:12312 | concerned makes with respect thereto representations in writing to
-- src:12313 | the public company, not exceeding a reasonable length, and requests
-- src:12314 | their notification to members of the company, the company must,
-- src:12315 | unless the representations are received by it too late for it to do so —
-- src:12317 | (a) in any notice of the resolution given to members of the
-- src:12318 | company state the fact of the representations having been
-- src:12319 | made; and
-- src:12321 | (b) send a copy of the representations to every member of the
-- src:12322 | company to whom notice of the meeting is sent, whether
-- src:12323 | before or after receipt of the representations by the
-- src:12324 | company,
-- src:12326 | and if a copy of the representations is not so sent because they were
-- src:12327 | received too late or because of the company’s default the director
-- src:12328 | may, without affecting the director’s right to be heard orally, require
-- src:12329 | that the representations must be read out at the meeting.
@ref s 152(3) (src:12311-12329)
GIVEN `notice is given pursuant to subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director makes representations in writing to the public company, not exceeding a reasonable length` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director requests their notification to members of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the representations are received by the company too late for it to notify them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 152(3) the company must notify the members of the representations` MEANS
    IF    `notice is given pursuant to subsection (2)`
      AND `the director makes representations in writing to the public company, not exceeding a reasonable length`
      AND `the director requests their notification to members of the company`
      AND (NOT `the representations are received by the company too late for it to notify them`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where notice is given pursuant to subsection (2) and the director concerned makes ... representations ... and requests their notification to members of the company, the company must, unless the representations are received by it too late for it to do so" -- a "where" gate (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b)) or the "unless" is not met

@ref s 152(3) (src:12326-12329)
GIVEN `a copy of the representations is not sent because they were received too late` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy of the representations is not sent because of the company's default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 152(3) the director may require that the representations be read out at the meeting` MEANS
    IF `a copy of the representations is not sent because they were received too late` OR `a copy of the representations is not sent because of the company's default`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- without affecting the director's right to be heard orally
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if a copy of the representations is not so sent because they were received too late or because of the company's default the director may ... require" -- a grant ("may") whose "if" gate failed (grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork line in NOTES.md)

-- (4) despite (1) to (3), copies need not be sent and the representations need not be read out if, on application of the public company or any other aggrieved person,
-- the Court is satisfied that the rights are being abused to secure needless publicity for defamatory matter; the Court may order the company's costs paid by the director.
-- src:12333 | (4) Despite subsections (1), (2) and (3), copies of the
-- src:12334 | representations need not be sent out and the representations need
-- src:12335 | not be read out at the meeting if, on the application either of the public
-- src:12336 | company or of any other person who claims to be aggrieved, the
-- src:12337 | Court is satisfied that the rights conferred by this section are being
-- src:12338 | abused to secure needless publicity for defamatory matter and the
-- src:12339 | Court may order the company’s costs on an application under this
-- src:12340 | section to be paid in whole or in part by the director, even though the
-- src:12341 | director is not a party to the application.
@ref s 152(4) (src:12333-12341)
GIVEN `the application is made by the public company or by any other person who claims to be aggrieved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied that the rights conferred by section 152 are being abused to secure needless publicity for defamatory matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 152(4) copies of the representations need not be sent out and the representations need not be read out` MEANS
    IF `the application is made by the public company or by any other person who claims to be aggrieved` AND `the Court is satisfied that the rights conferred by section 152 are being abused to secure needless publicity for defamatory matter`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "copies of the representations need not be sent out and the representations need not be read out if, on the application ..., the Court is satisfied that the rights ... are being abused" -- a condition introduced with "if" that fails (marginal reading (a), fork line in NOTES.md)

@ref s 152(4) (src:12338-12341)
GIVEN `the application is made by the public company or by any other person who claims to be aggrieved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied that the rights conferred by section 152 are being abused to secure needless publicity for defamatory matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 152(4) the Court may order the company's costs to be paid in whole or in part by the director` MEANS
    IF `the application is made by the public company or by any other person who claims to be aggrieved` AND `the Court is satisfied that the rights conferred by section 152 are being abused to secure needless publicity for defamatory matter`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- even though the director is not a party to the application
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if ... the Court is satisfied ... and the Court may order the company's costs" -- a grant ("may") whose "if" gate failed (grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork line in NOTES.md)

-- (5) a vacancy created by the removal of a director of a public company, if not filled at the meeting, may be filled as a casual vacancy.
-- src:12345 | (5) A vacancy created by the removal of a director of a public
-- src:12346 | company under this section, if not filled at the meeting at which the
-- src:12347 | director is removed, may be filled as a casual vacancy.
@ref s 152(5) (src:12345-12347)
GIVEN `the vacancy is created by the removal of a director of a public company under section 152` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the vacancy is not filled at the meeting at which the director is removed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 152(5) the vacancy may be filled as a casual vacancy` MEANS
    IF `the vacancy is created by the removal of a director of a public company under section 152` AND `the vacancy is not filled at the meeting at which the director is removed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A vacancy created by the removal of a director of a public company under this section, if not filled at the meeting ..., may be filled as a casual vacancy" -- a grant ("may") whose "if" gate failed (grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork line in NOTES.md)

-- (6) a person appointed in place of a person removed is treated, for the time at which the person or any other director is to retire, as if he or she had become a director on the day the removed person was last appointed.
-- src:12351 | (6) A person appointed director of a public company in place of a
-- src:12352 | person removed under this section is to be treated, for the purpose of
-- src:12357 | determining the time at which he or she or any other director is to
-- src:12358 | retire, as if he or she had become a director on the day on which the
-- src:12359 | person in whose place he or she is appointed was last appointed a
-- src:12360 | director.
@ref s 152(6) (src:12351-12360)
GIVEN `the person is appointed director of a public company in place of a person removed under section 152` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the person removed was last appointed a director` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 152(6) the day on which the replacement is treated as having become a director for the purpose of determining the time to retire` MEANS
    IF `the person is appointed director of a public company in place of a person removed under section 152`
    THEN JUST `the day on which the person removed was last appointed a director`
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person appointed director of a public company in place of a person removed under this section" -- a scope limit with no "only"

-- (7) nothing in (1) to (6) deprives a person removed of compensation or damages, or derogates from any power to remove that exists apart from the section.
-- src:12364 | (7) Nothing in subsections (1) to (6) is to be taken as depriving a
-- src:12365 | person removed as a director of a public company thereunder of
-- src:12366 | compensation or damages payable to him or her in respect of the
-- src:12367 | termination of his or her appointment as director or of any
-- src:12368 | appointment terminating with that as director or as derogating from
-- src:12369 | any power to remove a director which may exist apart from this
-- src:12370 | section.
@ref s 152(7) (src:12364-12370)
GIVEN `compensation or damages are payable to the person in respect of the termination of his or her appointment as director or of any appointment terminating with that as director` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 152(7) the removal deprives the person of compensation or damages payable in respect of the termination of the appointment` MEANS
    IF `compensation or damages are payable to the person in respect of the termination of his or her appointment as director or of any appointment terminating with that as director`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in subsections (1) to (6) is to be taken as depriving a person removed as a director of a public company thereunder of compensation or damages payable to him or her in respect of the termination of his or her appointment"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of compensation or damages payable and says nothing of other loss

@ref s 152(7) (src:12369-12370)
GIVEN `a power to remove a director exists apart from section 152` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 152(7) the section derogates from a power to remove a director which exists apart from the section` MEANS
    IF `a power to remove a director exists apart from section 152`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in subsections (1) to (6) is to be taken ... as derogating from any power to remove a director which may exist apart from this section"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of a power that exists apart from the section

-- (8) a director of a public company must not be removed by, or required to vacate office by reason of, any resolution, request or notice of the directors or any of them.
-- src:12374 | (8) A director of a public company must not be removed by, or be
-- src:12375 | required to vacate his or her office by reason of, any resolution,
-- src:12376 | request or notice of the directors or any of them despite anything in
-- src:12377 | the constitution or any agreement.
@ref s 152(8) (src:12374-12377)
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director would be removed, or required to vacate office, by a resolution, request or notice of the directors or any of them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 152(8) the subsection bars the directors from removing a director of a public company by their resolution, request or notice` MEANS
    IF `s 4(1) "public company" the company is a public company` TRUE `the company is a private company` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the director would be removed, or required to vacate office, by a resolution, request or notice of the directors or any of them`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- despite anything in the constitution or any agreement
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A director of a public company must not be removed by, or be required to vacate his or her office by reason of, any resolution, request or notice of the directors or any of them" -- a scope limit with no "only"

-- (9) subject to the constitution, a private company may by ordinary resolution remove a director before the expiration of his or her period of office despite any agreement.
-- src:12381 | (9) Subject to any provision to the contrary in the constitution, a
-- src:12382 | private company may by ordinary resolution remove a director before
-- src:12383 | the expiration of his or her period of office despite anything in any
-- src:12384 | agreement between the private company and the director.
@ref s 152(9) (src:12381-12384)
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the constitution contains a provision to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the kind of resolution passed` IS A `Kind of resolution`
      `the director is removed before the expiration of his or her period of office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 152(9) the private company may remove the director by ordinary resolution` MEANS
    IF `the constitution contains a provision to the contrary`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Subject to any provision to the contrary in the constitution" hands the question to the constitution, which is not among the sources; a grant ("may") whose gate is met by the constitution (grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork line in NOTES.md)
    ELSE (IF `the company is a private company` AND `the kind of resolution passed` EQUALS `an ordinary resolution` AND `the director is removed before the expiration of his or her period of office`
          THEN JUST TRUE   -- despite anything in any agreement between the private company and the director
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a private company may by ordinary resolution remove a director before the expiration of his or her period of office" -- a grant ("may") limited to a private company, an ordinary resolution and removal before expiry

DECLARE `s 152(2) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 152(2) send a copy of the notice of the intended resolution to the director concerned`

-- (2): the company must immediately send a copy. "Immediately" is not a number of days, so the rule has no time limit a trace can miss: no breach path (NOTES.md).
-- src:12299 | is removed, and on receipt of notice of an intended resolution to
-- src:12300 | remove a director under subsection (1) the company must
-- src:12305 | immediately send a copy thereof to the director concerned, and the
-- src:12306 | director, whether or not he or she is a member of the company, is
-- src:12307 | entitled to be heard on the resolution at the meeting.
@ref s 152(2) (src:12299-12307)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 152(2) act`
`s 152(2) a public company must send a copy of the notice of an intended removal to the director` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 152(2) send a copy of the notice of the intended resolution to the director concerned`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 152(2) gives this duty no deadline in days (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
